{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "יהושע בן נון העומד לפניך", :translit "yehoshua ben nun ha'omed lefanekha", :gloss "Joshua son of Nun, the one standing before you"} {:he "שגדולה שמושה יותר מלמודה", :translit "shegedulah shimusho yoter milimudo", :gloss "that his serving is greater than his learning"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Reading העומד לפניך as proof-text for shimush (serving a sage) over study."}], :frame {:text "The phrase העומד לפניך, 'who stands before you,' is read as praise of Joshua's role as attendant to Moses. The Talmud states that serving a Torah scholar is greater than studying from him: שמושן של תלמידי חכמים יותר מלמודן, and Joshua is cited as the paradigm since Scripture emphasizes that he 'did not depart from the tent' (Exodus 33:11) and here 'stands before' Moses. The term shimush denotes attending upon a sage to observe conduct and absorb practical halakhah beyond what formal study transmits.", :sources ["Berakhot 7b" "Exodus 33:11" "Deuteronomy 1:38"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Reading העומד לפניך as proof-text for shimush (serving a sage) over study.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:34:09.732328832Z", :model "glm-5.2"}